@startuml agentic-value-stream-semantic-boundary-matrix
' Per CR-VAS-003 §22 (Semantic Boundary Matrix).
' Cardinal author rule: Emmanuel A. Otchere <emmanuel@otchere.com>
' Last revised: 2026-10-08.

title Agentic Value Stream ; Semantic Boundary Matrix

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Helvetica"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false

note as N1
  Normative guidance matrix per CR-VAS-003 §22.

  A "+/-" denotes a borderline case where the
  criterion MAY be present but is not sufficient
  on its own to constitute the construct.

  Agentic participation is the only construct in
  this matrix that satisfies ALL five criteria
  simultaneously, which is why it alone qualifies
  as the realization relationship for AVS.
end note

object "Deterministic\nautomation" as DA
object "AI recommendation" as AIR
object "Human discretion" as HD
object "Agentic\nparticipation" as AP
object "Autonomous\nsystem" as AS
object "Workflow" as WF
object "AI system\n(generic)" as AIS

DA : Has objective = +/-
DA : Uses context = No
DA : Selects action = No
DA : Bounded authority = No/implicit
DA : Material VS effect = Yes

AIR : Has objective = No
AIR : Uses context = Yes
AIR : Selects action = No
AIR : Bounded authority = No
AIR : Material VS effect = Potential

HD : Has objective = Yes
HD : Uses context = Yes
HD : Selects action = Yes
HD : Bounded authority = Yes
HD : Material VS effect = Yes

AP : Has objective = Yes
AP : Uses context = Yes
AP : Selects action = Yes
AP : Bounded authority = Yes
AP : Material VS effect = Yes

AS : Has objective = Potential
AS : Uses context = Yes
AS : Selects action = Yes
AS : Bounded authority = Variable
AS : Material VS effect = Not necessarily

WF : Has objective = No
WF : Uses context = Limited
WF : Selects action = No
WF : Bounded authority = No
WF : Material VS effect = Potential

AIS : Has objective = Variable
AIS : Uses context = Variable
AIS : Selects action = Variable
AIS : Bounded authority = Variable
AIS : Material VS effect = Variable

@enduml
